## The question
One bench-scale FG-1 gate leaf at bulk 480 class, built as the
aluminium-skin / foam-core sandwich of EQS-1024/1037/1038, is weighed
and measured BLIND. Does its measured seat hold PENDING?

## Preregistration (locked before any article exists)
- PENDING window (locked): bulk (342.6, 500.1) kg/m3, equivalently
  split (17.6247, 17.7192). Design seat of the test article: split
  17.7089 (bulk 480).
- CLASS KILL: measured bulk >= 500.1 (already in shell) or <= 342.6
  (never enters) - the PENDING claim dies.
- SEAT KILL: measured split differing from 17.7089 by more than
  3 sigma of the bench budget (+-0.0038 nats) - the exact
  seat claim dies (the class may survive on the window alone, and is
  reported as such, separately).
- CONTROL KILLS: FG-1/B0 must audit NONE and FG-1/B2 must audit
  SPENT from their own measured (M, rho); a wrong control class
  kills the window placement, and with it the test verdict.

